  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Nortoxiferine, dihydro- interacts with the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14, which in turn targets KB. This interaction is supported by multiple pathways, with varying levels of confidence, as indicated by the final scores. The 26S proteasome subunit 14 is a common target across different compounds, including Kaempferol 3-O-D-Galactoside and Npc141945, both of which also target KB. This indicates a potential role for the 26S proteasome subunit 14 in mediating the effects of these compounds on KB. The evidence suggests that Nortoxiferine, dihydro- may exert its biological effects through this pathway, potentially modulating the activity of the 26S proteasome subunit 14 and subsequently influencing KB. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of the 26S proteasome subunit 14 as a central mediator in the relationship between Nortoxiferine, dihydro- and KB."
